From 07ab9ad7cb7a98e19346b2c62ca52581ad4e674e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:34:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aegisos: fix Utils.isProfileOrDeviceOwner to use
 getUsersForUiDisplay

The 3-arg overload (UserManager, DevicePolicyManager, String) iterated
the raw, unfiltered UserManager#getUsers() to look up each user's
profile-owner status. Four callers across Settings' legacy and Compose
App Info screens (AppButtonsPreferenceController, AppButtonRepository,
AppDisableButton, AppInfoSettingsMoreOptions) feed this into an
uninstall/disable button's enabled state with no admin gate protecting
any of them, unlike the sibling AppInfoDashboardFragment check that
already guards its own getUsers() call behind isAdminUser(). Found
while tracing exhaustive-audit item 16 (which only cited
AppButtonsPreferenceController.java:469): the audit's premise that this
call site might be moot if the decoy is non-admin does not hold here,
since this method has no admin gate at all, and the fix also closes
three additional call sites in the Compose SPA App Info screens that
the original 21-item audit missed entirely.

Fixed by using getUsersForUiDisplay(true), matching the pattern already
used for every other AegisOS Duress Unlock decoy-session fix in this
branch. isDeviceOwnerAppOnAnyUser() is left unscoped since it is a
genuine device-wide security control, not a per-user display concern.
---
 src/com/android/settings/Utils.java | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/settings/Utils.java b/src/com/android/settings/Utils.java
index bb89d6d..0cd1521 100644
--- a/src/com/android/settings/Utils.java
+++ b/src/com/android/settings/Utils.java
@@ -1129,7 +1129,13 @@ public final class Utils extends com.android.settingslib.Utils {
      */
     public static boolean isProfileOrDeviceOwner(UserManager userManager,
             DevicePolicyManager devicePolicyManager, String packageName) {
-        final List<UserInfo> userInfos = userManager.getUsers();
+        // getUsersForUiDisplay(true) is getUsers()'s own semantics plus AegisOS Duress
+        // Unlock decoy-session filtering: without it, this method's boolean result (and thus
+        // every caller's uninstall/disable button state) would depend on whether the real
+        // owner's own profile owns the package, leaking that another real user exists during
+        // a decoy session. isDeviceOwnerAppOnAnyUser() below is intentionally left unscoped:
+        // it is a genuine device-wide security control, not a per-user display concern.
+        final List<UserInfo> userInfos = userManager.getUsersForUiDisplay(true);
         if (devicePolicyManager.isDeviceOwnerAppOnAnyUser(packageName)) {
             return true;
         }
